{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum","id":375962,"title":"does prime 3 allow you to spend more quintessence than avatar minimum?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-20T01:20:16-08:00","id":375962,"title":"does prime 3 allow you to spend more quintessence than avatar minimum?","content":"as i interpret the rules it allows you to do so but only in the sense of transferring it somewhere or between patterns. e.g making tass giving it to an ally. ordraining it from a spirit/splat.<br /> <br /> but it does not help spending in the sense of &quot;burning&quot; it and disappearing after you use it. e.g to lower a difficulty or to power a spell like holy stroke or gabriel's embrace,<br /> <br /> also seaking of lower difficulties i'm correct in assuming that -3+3 is the maximum for all cases right? even ones not mentioned in the core book chart.<br /> <br /> e.g -2 difficulty on entropy in undeworld,-1or 2 on transforming your self while having one merit in the verbena book etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T03:25:04-08:00","id":376024,"title":"","content":"Prime allows you to Store more Quintessence in your Pattern than your Avatar Rating, you can Spend more than your Avatar rating too. You can draw Quint from a node via meditation over time etc to get it to those excess levels and your can also rip it direct from a Node too to power an effect (this damages the Node). It also lets you mess around with Tass yes.<br /> <br /> The +3/-3 thing is Net modifiers on a casting roll for a Magical Effect, outside modifiers still applying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T05:14:25-08:00","id":376077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=376024#post376024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime allows you to Store more Quintessence in your Pattern than your Avatar Rating, you can Spend more than your Avatar rating too. You can draw Quint from a node via meditation over time etc to get it to those excess levels and your can also rip it direct from a Node too to power an effect (this damages the Node). It also lets you mess around with Tass yes.<br /> <br /> The +3/-3 thing is Net modifiers on a casting roll for a Magical Effect, outside modifiers still applying.</div> </div> </div> </div>outside modifers meaning?<br /> <br /> <br /> and how does prime 3 work exactly&quot;? do i add prime 3 to what ever magical effect im already trying? or in case im using prime already do i just attempt to roll more successes? or do cast it with a duration on a node or some pieces of tass and when i want to spend quintessence these are spent automatically?<br /> <br /> also are you 100% positive on this? can you tell me in which book does it say so?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T07:34:55-08:00","id":376184,"title":"","content":"So normally Avatar determines two things (mostly): <br /> <br /> 1) Your natural Quintessence pool. This is the amount your pattern will naturally hold (replenished by meditating in a Node or similar), and it can not be taken from you easily (if at all).<br /> 2) Your ability to channel Quintessence. This is the limit on the amount of raw universal power your Avatar can handle at one time.<br /> <br /> <br /> So with Prime 1 you can store more Quintessence in your pattern than normal.<br /> With Prime 1 you can dip into your Life (health levels) for additional emergency Quintessence.<br /> <br /> Prime 3 allows you to channel Quintessence between things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I am not 100% sure of the canon ruling on this - but I personally do not believe any level of Prime (I never use 6+) can allow you to override this channel limit. It doesn't make sense for me.<br /> <br /> If you needed to pour 20 points of Quintessence into a Thing, and you had a Place to get it... Prime 3 would let you do that (basically). However... since your Avatar can only handle X Quintessence at a time, you will need to take your time to do it. <br /> <br /> Assume Avatar 2<br /> If you first go suck it all up with Prime, (bringing your total to 22 points) you will carry all that power in your pattern. You'll glow like a Christmas tree to anyone who can see it - but that's a side effect.<br /> <br /> Now you go start pouring all that stored power into a Thing. It doesn't make sense that Prime (which is a Sphere tied to the Avatar) would allow you to immediately dump 20 points through a 2 point Avatar... that seems like it would overwhelm him (possibly a precursor to a Gilgul rote). It does make sense to spend 10 turns channeling that power into the Thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Long story short: Using Prime 1 to overcome the Quintessence &quot;stored in pattern&quot; limit makes sense. Using Prime 3 to overcome the Avatar &quot;can only work with so much at once&quot; limit does not.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bNot sure if the books contradict me, but this is how it all sits in my head at the moment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T09:11:33-08:00","id":376312,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's how I rule it as well. Prime 1 is for storing Quintessence above the Avatar rating, Prime 3 is for moving it around, at a rate capped by your Avatar trait. Spending Quintessence is likewise capped by the Avatar.<br /> <br /> There is a ruling that allows you to get around this (from the Revised Storytellers Handbook) - you can substitute your Prime rating for your Avatar rating. So if you had Prime 4, you could channel up to 4 points of Quintessence per round. But I'm similarly not aware of anything that allows you to avoid caps entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T09:54:25-08:00","id":376350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=376312#post376312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's how I rule it as well. Prime 1 is for storing Quintessence above the Avatar rating, Prime 3 is for moving it around, at a rate capped by your Avatar trait. Spending Quintessence is likewise capped by the Avatar.<br /> <br /> There is a ruling that allows you to get around this (from the Revised Storytellers Handbook) - you can substitute your Prime rating for your Avatar rating. So if you had Prime 4, you could channel up to 4 points of Quintessence per round. But I'm similarly not aware of anything that allows you to avoid caps entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> At my table, I would be okay with this. It makes some logical sense, doesn't completely destroy the scale (still 1-5), and gives powerful mages a way to overcome their natural disadvantage (high Prime, low Avatar). Since I don't use Revised often I have always stuck to the Avatar limit, with a minimum of 1 per 2 turns (for those super rare Avatar 0 mages). I might consider changing to this Revised rule though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T10:33:43-08:00","id":376376,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I quite liked it for those reasons too. I use the rule, but it's a complete irrelevance in my current troupe, as they all have whacking great Avatar scores, lol. I tweaked Avatar a little so it's not such a one-tone trait (you regain your Avatar rating in Quintessence once per month, as your Avatar naturally refreshes itself - a small touch stolen from Awakening).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T16:56:31-08:00","id":376717,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Prime's quite useful once you realise that it allows you to muck about with huge reserves. Avatar is a nice crutch that helps you with raw power, but Prime does wonders to showcase how good a Mage works with some preparation and a good source of quintessence.<br /> <br /> I've also always judged that Mages can spent at least 1 Quint per turn even without the avatar background or Prime. One per two turns is just... too harsh. It's not like a low avatar rating means you're less of a Mage, just that it's not as easy as it might be for some others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T17:30:46-08:00","id":376732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=376077#post376077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">outside modifers meaning?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what Moirdryd is referring to is the idea that, because the +3/-3 limit is on the NET (final) modifier, you can actually spend more than 3 Quintessence as long as you are canceling out penalties.<br /> <br /> For example, if you have Avatar 5, and your Effect roll is suffering 1 point of penalty, you would be allowed to spend up to 4 Quintessence on the Effect. 1 point cancels the penalty, and 3 more give you a net modifier of -3 difficulty. In theory, Avatar 5 would let you spend 1 more point, but you can't lower the difficulty any further at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T22:10:46-08:00","id":376938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=376184#post376184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So normally Avatar determines two things (mostly):<br /> <br /> 1) Your natural Quintessence pool. This is the amount your pattern will naturally hold (replenished by meditating in a Node or similar), and it can not be taken from you easily (if at all).<br /> 2) Your ability to channel Quintessence. This is the limit on the amount of raw universal power your Avatar can handle at one time.<br /> <br /> <br /> So with Prime 1 you can store more Quintessence in your pattern than normal.<br /> With Prime 1 you can dip into your Life (health levels) for additional emergency Quintessence.<br /> <br /> Prime 3 allows you to channel Quintessence between things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I am not 100% sure of the canon ruling on this - but I personally do not believe any level of Prime (I never use 6+) can allow you to override this channel limit. It doesn't make sense for me.<br /> <br /> If you needed to pour 20 points of Quintessence into a Thing, and you had a Place to get it... Prime 3 would let you do that (basically). However... since your Avatar can only handle X Quintessence at a time, you will need to take your time to do it.<br /> <br /> Assume Avatar 2<br /> If you first go suck it all up with Prime, (bringing your total to 22 points) you will carry all that power in your pattern. You'll glow like a Christmas tree to anyone who can see it - but that's a side effect.<br /> <br /> Now you go start pouring all that stored power into a Thing. It doesn't make sense that Prime (which is a Sphere tied to the Avatar) would allow you to immediately dump 20 points through a 2 point Avatar... that seems like it would overwhelm him (possibly a precursor to a Gilgul rote). It does make sense to spend 10 turns channeling that power into the Thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Long story short: Using Prime 1 to overcome the Quintessence &quot;stored in pattern&quot; limit makes sense. Using Prime 3 to overcome the Avatar &quot;can only work with so much at once&quot; limit does not.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bNot sure if the books contradict me, but this is how it all sits in my head at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> first of all i think your avatar rating does not add to the quintessence pool. it stays at 20 no matter what i think. it's just that your first 1-5 points are protected by the avatar.<br /> after all doesn't the core book say that you can meditate at nodes to rechard <b>if your pool is lower than your avatar rating</b> .i think the only npcs with more than 20 points were voormas and al aswad . but the former had an avatar rating of 8 while the later was a walkingplot device power<br /> <br /> also how does someone with 0 avatar makes a wonder? hell most of the prime sphere becomes completely useless if you ask me.<br /> that's why i always assumed that there is a difference in spending(as in burning it all completely for instance when you are healing aggravated damage ) and spending as in moving it around. after all a wonder has quintessence inside it right? so technically it's not spent as in destroyed.<br /> <br /> it's just that the core book is not clear at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T23:23:45-08:00","id":377000,"title":"","content":"i so hope m20 takes te approach of fountin dark ages. where even a 0 rating allow you to spend some quintessence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T02:04:45-08:00","id":377052,"title":"","content":"With prime you can spend as much quintessence as you have successes. With Prime you can also bring a shitload of tass (Quintessence that took on physical form) and then channel it all into a spell or an item. So yeah, not having a very strong avatar just means you need to prepare better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T07:34:04-08:00","id":377222,"title":"","content":"@Asmodai<br /> <br /> You might be right that 1/2 per turn is too little. In reality, I have had this situation come up exactly once and it was a semi-NPC that a PC played sometimes (an out of towner). If I had more experience with Avatar 0 mages I might make that adjustment... though I really think I prefer the Prime limit proposed in Revised.<br /> <br /> <br /> @mark<br /> <br /> You're right! I wasn't even thinking about the 20 upper limit, was just doing some adding for the example. Good catch.<br /> <br /> On to your point about burning it all... I would retort that even healing aggravated damage should abide by the limit, and thus require more time and effort than healing lethal. That's how I've always done it and it isn't a huge deal... it does make mages squishier than other supernaturals, but I think they should be. <br /> <br /> &quot;Burning&quot; and &quot;Moving&quot; are the same thing though. When you use it to heal aggravated damage, you aren't burning it as much as you are moving it around to reform your pattern - since without fixing the damaged pattern the body will never heal.<br /> <br /> Casting a fireball isn't &quot;burning&quot; it either, since the essence becomes the fireball and then mingles with the target pattern to cause damage (to the pattern).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T09:50:40-08:00","id":377289,"title":"","content":"Can Prime be used to raise your own Avatar rating?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T10:19:08-08:00","id":377343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=377289#post377289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Prime be used to raise your own Avatar rating?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say no. At the very least (in my mind) you would need Prime 5, Spirit 5, Correspondence 5... and I would still make it a huge sub-plot or even main plot.<br /> <br /> There is only one canon way to improve it: resolving the Shattered Avatar flaw. Outside of that, improving Avatar is a wholly RP related thing. If it makes sense for the story, then so be it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T01:20:24-08:00","id":377882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=377222#post377222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Asmodai<br /> <br /> You might be right that 1/2 per turn is too little. In reality, I have had this situation come up exactly once and it was a semi-NPC that a PC played sometimes (an out of towner). If I had more experience with Avatar 0 mages I might make that adjustment... though I really think I prefer the Prime limit proposed in Revised.<br /> <br /> <br /> @mark<br /> <br /> You're right! I wasn't even thinking about the 20 upper limit, was just doing some adding for the example. Good catch.<br /> <br /> On to your point about burning it all... I would retort that even healing aggravated damage should abide by the limit, and thus require more time and effort than healing lethal. That's how I've always done it and it isn't a huge deal... it does make mages squishier than other supernaturals, but I think they should be.<br /> <br /> &quot;Burning&quot; and &quot;Moving&quot; are the same thing though. When you use it to heal aggravated damage, you aren't burning it as much as you are moving it around to reform your pattern - since without fixing the damaged pattern the body will never heal.<br /> <br /> Casting a fireball isn't &quot;burning&quot; it either, since the essence becomes the fireball and then mingles with the target pattern to cause damage (to the pattern).</div> </div> </div> </div>does casting a fireball really require you to usequintessence?? i thought prime 2 takes care of this.<br /> <br /> unless theres some method to do it just by forces 3?<br /> <br /> i mean otherwise you might as well just use holy stroke with just prime 2 . and much lower difficulty","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T02:19:35-08:00","id":377906,"title":"","content":"No spell you are casting has quintessence as a mandatory requirement. What prime is used is if you seek to create something out of nothing (i.e. giant honking ball of explosive flame). You can use forces 3, but you need a source first - i.e. you could use Forces 3 to use a house on fire to create a vortex of flame that will murder everything in the street. Or you could make gas pipes rapture and ignite with Forces 3.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 is a &quot;easier&quot; source of Aggravated damage, but...<br /> a) you don't really always have to use aggravated damage<br /> b) Forces is more efficient, remember that it gives you extra damage for all effects based of Forces","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T02:30:28-08:00","id":377914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=377906#post377906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No spell you are casting has quintessence as a mandatory requirement. What prime is used is if you seek to create something out of nothing (i.e. giant honking ball of explosive flame). You can use forces 3, but you need a source first - i.e. you could use Forces 3 to use a house on fire to create a vortex of flame that will murder everything in the street. Or you could make gas pipes rapture and ignite with Forces 3.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 is a &quot;easier&quot; source of Aggravated damage, but...<br /> a) you don't really always have to use aggravated damage<br /> b) Forces is more efficient, remember that it gives you extra damage for all effects based of Forces</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> but forces fire is also aggravated right? and we're taling about just one point of extra damage(in revised)<br /> <br /> plus prime 2 will actually cause more damage because it's difficulty is 4(vulgar no witnesses) +2.<br /> <br /> a fire ball is 4+3+1=8","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T03:15:37-08:00","id":377922,"title":"","content":"Fire... is usually aggravated. That doesn't mean that it's always aggravated, though.<br /> <br /> The difference is 6 vs. 7, not 6 vs. 8.<br /> Also consider that Forces adds one Success, not one dice of damage. One Success on casting can mean a huge margin, especially considering how damage is caused by spells (dice vs. levels and/or multiplication)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T03:41:05-08:00","id":377933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=377922#post377922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fire... is usually aggravated. That doesn't mean that it's always aggravated, though.<br /> <br /> The difference is 6 vs. 7, not 6 vs. 8.<br /> Also consider that Forces adds one Success, not one dice of damage. One Success on casting can mean a huge margin, especially considering how damage is caused by spells (dice vs. levels and/or multiplication)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> in whichcase would it not be aggravated?<br /> <br /> anyway according to the core rulebook revised it says&quot;forces always adds one level of damage&quot;<br /> <br /> youre right though the differences is 6vs 7. i was just thinking sth about dark ages mage at the moment and got confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T06:16:13-08:00","id":377987,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it was one success. I don't have the books at hand, but I can check when I get home.<br /> <br /> For instance Fire usually isn't aggravated for Mages. It's Lethal. And Mages cannot soak lethal damage and consider it as grievous and horrible wounds. The same fire would do aggravated to a Vampire and a Werewolf. In general the point of aggravated is that it's a form of damage with a deeper magical or spiritual component that makes these wounds bane and semipermanent to non-humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T06:26:08-08:00","id":377993,"title":"","content":"I probably should have chosen a better example than fireball. As Asmodai said you don't have to use Quintessence for a fireball, or virtually any spell really (some though...). My point was just the quintessence in the fireball (whether you spent a point or it was just ambient quintessence) isn't being destroyed, but rather moved around like a battering ram through other quintessence patterns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T07:49:26-08:00","id":378051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=377987#post377987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure it was one success. I don't have the books at hand, but I can check when I get home.<br /> <br /> For instance Fire usually isn't aggravated for Mages. It's Lethal. And Mages cannot soak lethal damage and consider it as grievous and horrible wounds. The same fire would do aggravated to a Vampire and a Werewolf. In general the point of aggravated is that it's a form of damage with a deeper magical or spiritual component that makes these wounds bane and semipermanent to non-humans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> according to the core rule book<br /> <br /> fire damage is always aggravated,that is the nature of fire. pg 248,<br /> <br /> force attacks inflict one extra level of damage automatically pg 209<br /> <br /> in the same page it gives an example of a mage blasting 2 targets with fire. it's aggravated<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> also it says charged with quntessencea ny attack is aggravated. does that mean that i can spend a point of quintessence to make a mind bashing attack aggravated? and do points used to lowerthe difficulty count?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T08:16:50-08:00","id":378072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=378051#post378051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> according to the core rule book<br /> <br /> fire damage is always aggravated,that is the nature of fire. pg 248,<br /> <br /> force attacks inflict one extra level of damage automatically pg 209<br /> <br /> in the same page it gives an example of a mage blasting 2 targets with fire. it's aggravated<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> also it says charged with quntessencea ny attack is aggravated. does that mean that i can spend a point of quintessence to make a mind bashing attack aggravated? and do points used to lowerthe difficulty count?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mind specifically is strange with damage. I actually don't know about that one... instead of making it aggravated damage I might say that it inflicts a permanent derangement (in addition to standard Mind damage).<br /> <br /> Points used to lower difficulty do not count. You must specifically spend a point to elevate the damage type, once per attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T08:35:58-08:00","id":378086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=378072#post378072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Mind specifically is strange with damage. I actually don't know about that one... instead of making it aggravated damage I might say that it inflicts a permanent derangement (in addition to standard Mind damage).<br /> <br /> Points used to lower difficulty do not count. You must specifically spend a point to elevate the damage type, once per attack.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> but other than mind or if you feel like using lightingbols or telekinetic blasts or gravity (normally lethal and bashing in the later 2 i assume ) instead of fire or laser beams. is there <b>any</b> direct attack that doesn't do aggravated damage on it's own?<br /> <br /> life 3 is aggravated. granted you can lower it to lethal or bashing if you want but why spend quintessence to let it do sth it already can? <br /> entropy 4 is aggravated. there are even rotes that prove it.<br /> fire has already been covered.<br /> prime is aggravated by definition.\\<br /> correspondence:well i suppose teleporting someone 200 meters in the air and letting him fall is lethal but it's a bit of a stretch to try to apply that rule here.<br /> time doesn't do direct damage neither does spirit.<br /> same goes for matter. though i suppose transmuting the air in soneone's lungs to stone would cause suffocation. but that's a matter for aother discussion.<br /> <br /> it's funny how the book says &quot;most spheres cause lethal damage&quot; but in practice it is different.<br /> <br /> the only way this rule makes sense is if it allows you to cause aggravated damage without it being vulgar. for isntance using life to cause bashing damage(frequently a coincidence) then charging the spel lqith quintessence but it appearing to an outside observer like a normal bashing wound.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T09:01:40-08:00","id":378102,"title":"","content":"Baseball bats don't do aggravated damage without Prime. Neither do bullets.<br /> <br /> Yes, Entropy 4 and Life 3 and all of that can be aggravated (usually vulgar). But for the low, low cost of Prime 2 (3 if you want to make them charms!) you can use a sniper rifle to deliver coincidental aggravated damage at 1000 yards.<br /> <br /> So while a mage who can rock your world with some direct magick is dangerous, a mage who can provide a team of sleepers with aggravated damage weapons and consumables is also very dangerous. Life 3 doesn't allow your acolytes to wield a night-stick that can hurt Vampires. Prime 3 does, if only temporarily. Prime 4 does, permanently. Prime 5 could let them lose the night-stick and deliver aggravated damage with their fists.<br /> <br /> Prime is still useful, even though it isn't the only useful Sphere.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Prime being used to make things aggravated isn't really aimed at magick, but at the mundane. By infusing something mundane with excess quintessence, it's kind of like driving nails into the end of a club... you are turning normal damage into magick aggravated damage. This really is a huge deal if you do a lot of crossover or &quot;mage on the street&quot; stuff, but less so if you are mostly focused on &quot;mage vs mage&quot; stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":2211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","user":"SixFootChicken","date":". 01-22-2015, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T09:10:55-08:00","id":378107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=378102#post378102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baseball bats don't do aggravated damage without Prime. Neither do bullets.<br /> <br /> Yes, Entropy 4 and Life 3 and all of that can be aggravated (usually vulgar). But for the low, low cost of Prime 2 (3 if you want to make them charms!) you can use a sniper rifle to deliver coincidental aggravated damage at 1000 yards.<br /> <br /> So while a mage who can rock your world with some direct magick is dangerous, a mage who can provide a team of sleepers with aggravated damage weapons and consumables is also very dangerous. Life 3 doesn't allow your acolytes to wield a night-stick that can hurt Vampires. Prime 3 does, if only temporarily. Prime 4 does, permanently. Prime 5 could let them lose the night-stick and deliver aggravated damage with their fists.<br /> <br /> Prime is still useful, even though it isn't the only useful Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> correct me if im wrong but temporarily enchanting a weapon doesn's cost quintessence. you're talkng about wonders here. though i suppose they technically count as charged with quintessence.<br /> <br /> prime may not be the only useful but in ascension it is the most useful sphere. at least it's lower levels. without prime 1 someone could give you a rock and swear to god it's tass. youcan have very little quintessence in your pool(one of the extremely few things i likes in dark ages mage was that it didn't do this) etc. i think that in awakening they gave all arcana a limited magic sensory capability jsut because of this. at least that's what people who play it tell me<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T12:53:07-08:00","id":378299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=378051#post378051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> according to the core rule book<br /> <br /> fire damage is always aggravated,that is the nature of fire. pg 248,<br /> <br /> force attacks inflict one extra level of damage automatically pg 209<br /> <br /> in the same page it gives an example of a mage blasting 2 targets with fire. it's aggravated<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> also it says charged with quntessencea ny attack is aggravated. does that mean that i can spend a point of quintessence to make a mind bashing attack aggravated? and do points used to lowerthe difficulty count?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah. You are right, but so am I <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I would have pointed you to the page 171 and we would have gone in circles around each other. You're going by Revised, my memory went from 2nd. The same applies to Fire on page 264. In 2nd ed Fire was not Aggravated by default to ordinary humans as ordinary humans weren't any more succeptible to fire then bullets or decapitation :P. I guess that stuck around as it felt reasonable, what with the Mages being quite squishy. The joys of playing a game through 16 years :P.<br /> <br /> Charged with Quintessence doesn't mean &quot;spend quintessence to do aggravated damage&quot;, it's a description of how Prime 2 works to enchant weapons to do horrible bodily harm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T13:51:15-08:00","id":378346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=378299#post378299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hah. You are right, but so am I <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I would have pointed you to the page 171 and we would have gone in circles around each other. You're going by Revised, my memory went from 2nd. The same applies to Fire on page 264. In 2nd ed Fire was not Aggravated by default to ordinary humans as ordinary humans weren't any more succeptible to fire then bullets or decapitation :P. I guess that stuck around as it felt reasonable, what with the Mages being quite squishy. The joys of playing a game through 16 years :P.<br /> <br /> Charged with Quintessence doesn't mean &quot;spend quintessence to do aggravated damage&quot;, it's a description of how Prime 2 works to enchant weapons to do horrible bodily harm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I agree that for normal sleepers fire should be lethal. It makes more sense to me. Otherwise Vampires are &quot;weak to fire - like everybody else, no more no less - to the point that they are deathly afraid of it and might completely go bat shit insane when confronted with it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T19:05:29-08:00","id":1015473,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the thread necro, but I recently ran into this problem.<br /> <br /> HDYDT says the character could &quot;employ in that effect&quot; quintessence above her arete based on the damaga&amp;duration chart. Fine and dandy, but which roll it is based on? Is she needing to roll another casting to see how much quintessence could be used on the next effect to lower diff, for example? If so, how long she could &quot;hold the charge&quot;? Or is it integrated into the main effect's roll? If so, how it could lower the diff? It's seems contradictory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T02:45:23-08:00","id":1015619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=1015473#post1015473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies for the thread necro, but I recently ran into this problem.<br /> <br /> HDYDT says the character could &quot;employ in that effect&quot; quintessence above her arete based on the damaga&amp;duration chart. Fine and dandy, but which roll it is based on? Is she needing to roll another casting to see how much quintessence could be used on the next effect to lower diff, for example? If so, how long she could &quot;hold the charge&quot;? Or is it integrated into the main effect's roll? If so, how it could lower the diff? It's seems contradictory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> you can't roll twice in a turn for a spell. it's part of the main effect.<br /> <br /> of course with time 4 entropy 1 you could create a hanging effect. or possibly make a wonder of &quot;charging quintessence&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T06:21:47-08:00","id":1015656,"title":"","content":"If you use a Prime 3 effect that gets say 4 successes you would be able to channel 6 quintessence above your Avatar rating into an effect during the duration of the scene. Now whether or not that could be done per turn, or as the total amount channelled for the scene is up to the ST but I would lean toward the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T09:09:05-08:00","id":1015691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=1015656#post1015656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you use a Prime 3 effect that gets say 4 successes you would be able to channel 6 quintessence above your Avatar rating into an effect during the duration of the scene. Now whether or not that could be done per turn, or as the total amount channelled for the scene is up to the ST but I would lean toward the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you count that as a separate effect with it's own casting roll, or would you add Prime 3 to the Spheres needed and make it one effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T10:35:04-08:00","id":1015728,"title":"","content":"As an addition to the existing effect would require many more successes but is doable. I like using is as a type of enhancing effect before the acutal effect it will be used on, eather way its more than likely going to be an extended ritual","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T12:56:25-08:00","id":1015793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=1015656#post1015656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you use a Prime 3 effect that gets say 4 successes you would be able to channel 6 quintessence above your Avatar rating into an effect during the duration of the scene. Now whether or not that could be done per turn, or as the total amount channelled for the scene is up to the ST but I would lean toward the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I was thinking about the same line, as handling it as separate effects. For some reasons, I counted the damage/duration chart as an either/or thing in this case, don't really know why. It makes sense if it is both.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T13:03:57-08:00","id":1015794,"title":"","content":"Damage duration chart is an either or. You use the successes one way or the other. 4 successes on a Prime 3 effect would count 3 succeses to quintessence manipulation, so 6 quintessence. 2 successes give you a scene (or is it a day?) of duraton with which to channel the energies. If you needed more than this then the Prime effect itself would probably be its own ritual and tou would need the duration to possibly be a few days or a week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T13:46:57-08:00","id":1015816,"title":"","content":"Ok, but in your example, you divided the successes between damage and duration, so it would use that chart isnted of the base damage&amp;duration one. So, for 4 success, it would be 4 quintessence and one scene, no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T13:52:05-08:00","id":1015819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=1015728#post1015728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an addition to the existing effect would require many more successes but is doable. I like using is as a type of enhancing effect before the acutal effect it will be used on, eather way its more than likely going to be an extended ritual</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it, I would probably see it as two castings. 1) Summon the power 2) USE IT.<br /> <br /> I doubt I would see it happening as two separate one round castings and actually accomplish much, but most casting in my games ends up being multi-phase progressive. First roll gets X success meaning the effect is doing thus and so.... if more is desired, keep rolling. Not really Rituals with all the prep and pomp (or, really structured behavior). More like just repeating the incantaions and gestures again and again until you get what you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T20:35:03-08:00","id":1015963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=1015816#post1015816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but in your example, you divided the successes between damage and duration, so it would use that chart isnted of the base damage&amp;duration one. So, for 4 success, it would be 4 quintessence and one scene, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both charts calculate damage as 2 levels for each success (well after 2 successes anyways) so 3 successes toward damage would be 6, so 6 quintessence. 1 success would be the scene on the dividing success chart. You would need 2 towards duration for a scene if using the base chart.<br /> <br /> Edit: I see where I counted wrong in my example, sorry. To do the way I originally posted would have needed 5 successes to count 3 and 2. Stupid math.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 12-11-2016, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T23:46:11-08:00","id":1016002,"title":"","content":"According to my reading of the rules the 6 quint in your spell are ready to be channeled once.<br /> For x quint per round you need the optional damage over duration chart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T05:24:33-08:00","id":1016073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/375962-does-prime-3-allow-you-to-spend-more-quintessence-than-avatar-minimum?p=1016002#post1016002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to my reading of the rules the 6 quint in your spell are ready to be channeled once.<br /> For x quint per round you need the optional damage over duration chart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why the effect splits successes between duration and damage.<br /> <br /> Edit: I see what chart you are referring to. I forget about that one. You could use it if you prefer, we just go off the base damage/duration chart as its on the same page and quicker with basically the same result. <br /> <br /> 1 problem I have with M20 is there is quite a few options for ways to run / handle things from background to mechanics so when we discuss things on the forum we all can be coming from various preferences of how we run our games. Of course it also gives us the greatest amount of leway to run our games the way we like best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 12-12-2016, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}